{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FUgfmvHQfJU8i5sf6TjN21","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\n     2→title: \"Build, lint, and version-check via mage targets\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs mage build to compile cmd/version to bin/version, verifies that the\n     6→  binary prints the repository's version tag, runs mage lint to confirm no warnings, and\n     7→  runs mage clean to remove build artifacts. This exercises the full build lifecycle\n     8→  specified in prd011-magefiles before any utility code exists.\n     9→\n    10→actor: Human Operator\n    11→\n    12→trigger: |\n    13→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd011-magefiles.yaml) and wants to verify that the\n    14→  build pipeline produces a working binary.\n    15→\n    16→flow:\n    17→  - id: F1\n    18→    step: |\n    19→      The operator runs mage build. The target compiles every package under cmd/ to bin/.\n    20→      For cmd/version, the target resolves the latest version tag via\n    21→      git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passes it through -ldflags.\n    22→  - id: F2\n    23→    step: |\n    24→      The operator runs bin/version. The binary prints the version tag (e.g., \"v0.20260228.0\")\n    25→      to stdout followed by a newline and exits 0.\n    26→  - id: F3\n    27→    step: |\n    28→      The operator runs bin/version --version. The output is identical to F2.\n    29→  - id: F4\n    30→    step: |\n    31→      The operator runs bin/version --bogus. The binary prints a usage message to stderr\n    32→      and exits 2.\n    33→  - id: F5\n    34→    step: |\n    35→      The operator runs mage lint. golangci-lint runs on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/ with\n    36→      no warnings or errors.\n    37→  - id: F6\n    38→    step: |\n    39→      The operator runs mage clean. The bin/ directory and its contents are removed. If\n    40→      bin/ does not exist, the target succeeds silently.\n    41→  - id: F7\n    42→    step: |\n    43→      The operator verifies that bin/ no longer exists after mage clean.\n    44→\n    45→touchpoints:\n    46→  - T1: \"cmd/version — version string printing, ldflags injection (prd011-magefiles R1)\"\n    47→  - T2: \"magefiles/ — build, lint, clean targets (prd011-magefiles R2, R3, R4)\"\n    48→  - T3: \"configuration.yaml — project.binary_dir, project.go_source_dirs (prd011-magefiles R6)\"\n    49→\n    50→success_criteria:\n    51→  - id: S1\n    52→    criterion: mage build succeeds and bin/version exists.\n    53→  - id: S2\n    54→    criterion: bin/version prints a version tag matching v[0-9]* and exits 0.\n    55→  - id: S3\n    56→    criterion: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n    57→  - id: S4\n    58→    criterion: bin/version --bogus prints to stderr and exits 2.\n    59→  - id: S5\n    60→    criterion: mage lint passes with no warnings on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/.\n    61→  - id: S6\n    62→    criterion: mage clean removes bin/ and succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n    63→  - id: S7\n    64→    criterion: A development build (no ldflags) produces a binary that prints \"dev\".\n    65→\n    66→out_of_scope:\n    67→  - Differential testing of cmd/version against a reference binary (there is no GNU version equivalent).\n    68→  - mage install is exercised by the operator manually; it is not part of this use case's primary flow.\n    69→  - Orchestrator, generator, scaffold, and prompt targets are provided by cobbler-scaffold and not covered here.\n    70→\n    71→test_suite: test-rel00.0\n    72→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ba7b611-6e9a-4a57-994c-cbdb7a7c6af5","uuid":"329be1b3-4d1c-4832-b91f-92dfc648315a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/242/docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc001-magefiles.yaml","content":"id: rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\ntitle: \"Build, lint, and version-check via mage targets\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs mage build to compile cmd/version to bin/version, verifies that the\n  binary prints the repository's version tag, runs mage lint to confirm no warnings, and\n  runs mage clean to remove build artifacts. This exercises the full build lifecycle\n  specified in prd011-magefiles before any utility code exists.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd011-magefiles.yaml) and wants to verify that the\n  build pipeline produces a working binary.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs mage build. The target compiles every package under cmd/ to bin/.\n      For cmd/version, the target resolves the latest version tag via\n      git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passes it through -ldflags.\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      The operator runs bin/version. The binary prints the version tag (e.g., \"v0.20260228.0\")\n      to stdout followed by a newline and exits 0.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      The operator runs bin/version --version. The output is identical to F2.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The operator runs bin/version --bogus. The binary prints a usage message to stderr\n      and exits 2.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The operator runs mage lint. golangci-lint runs on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/ with\n      no warnings or errors.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The operator runs mage clean. The bin/ directory and its contents are removed. If\n      bin/ does not exist, the target succeeds silently.\n  - id: F7\n    step: |\n      The operator verifies that bin/ no longer exists after mage clean.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/version — version string printing, ldflags injection (prd011-magefiles R1)\"\n  - T2: \"magefiles/ — build, lint, clean targets (prd011-magefiles R2, R3, R4)\"\n  - T3: \"configuration.yaml — project.binary_dir, project.go_source_dirs (prd011-magefiles R6)\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: mage build succeeds and bin/version exists.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: bin/version prints a version tag matching v[0-9]* and exits 0.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: bin/version --bogus prints to stderr and exits 2.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: mage lint passes with no warnings on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: mage clean removes bin/ and succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: A development build (no ldflags) produces a binary that prints \"dev\".\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Differential testing of cmd/version against a reference binary (there is no GNU version equivalent).\n  - mage install is exercised by the operator manually; it is not part of this use case's primary flow.\n  - Orchestrator, generator, scaffold, and prompt targets are provided by cobbler-scaffold and not covered here.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel00.0\n","numLines":72,"startLine":1,"totalLines":72}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012MPmKzGcEYphfydPEC5sRs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me analyze the requirements:\n\nFrom the PRD (prd011-magefiles):\n- R1.1: `cmd/version/` package, prints version string to stdout + newline, exits 0\n- R1.2: Version set via `-ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\"`, defaults to \"dev\"\n- R1.4: `--version` or `-v` prints same version; any other flag prints usage to stderr and exits 2\n- R1.5: Export a variable or function so other cmd/ packages can import\n\nFrom the task requirements:\n- R1: Print version info to stdout\n\n\n- R2: Support build-time injection via ldflags, default \"dev\"\n- R3: Handle SIGPIPE\n- R4: Exit 0 on success, exit 1 on write failure\n- R5: Copyright header, SPDX, package comment\n\nI'm settling on a package-level version variable that defaults to \"dev\", with a minimal main function that sets up SIGPIPE handling, writes the version to stdout using fmt.Fprintln, and exits appropriately based on success or write errors. Now let me reconsider R1.4 more carefully regarding flag handling.\n\nThe PRD requires that `--version` and `-v` print the same output as no arguments, while any unrecognized flag should print usage to stderr and exit with code 2. This means I need to add flag parsing logic to distinguish between valid version flags and invalid ones, rather than just printing the version unconditionally. requirements.\n\nLet me think about the flag parsing. R1.4 says:\n- `--version` or `-v` → print version\n- Any other flag → usage to stderr, exit 2\n\nThis is a bit tricky with Go's `flag` package. Let me think about how to implement this cleanly.\n\nActually, looking at it more carefully, I need to:\n1. Accept `--version` and `-v` flags\n2. Reject unknown flags (exit 2 with usage)\n3. No arguments → print version\n4. `--version` or `-v` → print version\n\nGo's `flag` package handles both `-version` and `--version` by stripping the leading dash, so defining a `version` flag covers both cases. I'll also add a separate `-v` flag. When `flag.Parse()` encounters an unknown flag, it automatically prints an error to stderr and exits with code 2, which is exactly what I need. So I'll set up custom usage output, define the version and v flags, call `flag.Parse()`, and then check which flag was set to print the version. I see there's a conflict between R1.5 (which requires the version to be exportable for other packages) and the constraint that this is `package main`. Looking at the architecture notes, it seems R1.5 might be outside the scope of what I'm actually implementing here—the task requirements only list R1 through R5, and they're all about the binary's behavior itself, not about making the version importable by other packages. Since I'm only creating `cmd/version/main.go` as a standalone binary, I'll focus on those core requirements and treat the version as internal to this package.\n\nNow I need to clarify the output format. The PRD specifies that the version command should print just the version tag string (like `v1.0.0` or `dev`) followed by a newline, but the task R1 mentions \"program name and version string.\" Let me check what the PRD actually requires here. The PRD is clear—just the version string, no program name. The use case confirms it's simply the version tag printed to stdout with a newline. Now I'm writing the Go code to implement this, starting with the package declaration and imports.\n\nWriting the version command... Setting up the flag parsing...\n\nI'm realizing the default flag behavior already handles unknown flags correctly—it exits with code 2 and prints an error, which matches what's needed. The flag package's `ExitOnError` mode takes care of that automatically, so I don't need to do anything special there.\n\nFor positional arguments, the spec doesn't mention them, so I'll just let them pass through without validation. And `-v` as a shorthand for version works fine since this is a standalone binary with no other flags to conflict with.\n\nThe implementation should satisfy all the acceptance criteria: it compiles, prints the version and exits cleanly, defaults to \"dev\", and will contain the injected version string when built with ldflags.\n\nWriting the implementation...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3856,"cache_read_input_tokens":46583,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3856},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ba7b611-6e9a-4a57-994c-cbdb7a7c6af5","uuid":"d4fddbc2-5468-447e-852e-b67b9d74e4ef"}
